From e82f09ce6868744351481f843b6f0259355c053f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Lintermann <rl@karo-electronics.de>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:56:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx219: rework timing setup and stream control

- Move the PLL clock table into the common register sequence and
  program the fixed line length (PPL 3448) up front
- Rename FLL to VTS and make hblank read-only, as PPL is fixed
- Select the binning mode inline from the format bpp and drop the
  separate binning/rate-factor helpers
- Apply a dedicated register sequence when streaming 1080p
- Replace enable/disable_streams with s_stream and require exactly
  one supported link-frequency on the endpoint
- Get xclk via devm_clk_get(), expose subdev events and set up
  runtime PM after subdev registration

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [karo-specific]

Generated by Mistral Vibe.
Co-Authored-By: Mistral Vibe <vibe@mistral.ai>
